WEBVTT

00:17.300 --> 00:18.770
GHOST BUSTERZ!

00:17.660 --> 00:20.410
OH! The time has come

00:18.200 --> 00:18.770
BUSTERZ!

00:20.410 --> 00:23.800
To stand up for tomorrow

00:22.760 --> 00:24.200
OH OH OH!

00:23.800 --> 00:26.360
We're ghostbusterz

00:26.360 --> 00:31.010
Breakin' away from the old ghosts

00:31.010 --> 00:34.380
Of history

00:34.380 --> 00:37.760
Breaking free!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

01:13.240 --> 01:17.060
No fear for anything in our way!

01:15.670 --> 01:20.470
Presented by hwat fansubs

01:17.060 --> 01:18.610
The time has come

01:33.110 --> 01:37.330
The seventh month of 1600 AD, or Keicho 5.

01:37.700 --> 01:41.500
Charging Tokugawa Ieyasu with thirteen articles of impeachment,

01:41.500 --> 01:48.420
Ishida Mitsunari sent messengers to various daimyo in the name of the Toyotomi clan,

01:48.420 --> 01:51.590
telling them to raise armies.

01:51.590 --> 01:56.680
At the same time, beings seeking to end the period of turbulence

01:56.680 --> 02:00.560
and build a kingdom to last a thousand years

02:00.560 --> 02:04.810
were about to awaken from a thousand-year sleep.

02:04.810 --> 02:06.810
And then...

02:06.810 --> 02:10.570
On the fifteenth day of the ninth month, at Sekigahara,

02:10.570 --> 02:13.030
the Eastern Army of Tokugawa Ieyasu clashed with

02:13.030 --> 02:18.160
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and Ishida Mitsunari.

02:18.160 --> 02:21.620
As a result of the performance of Kobayakawa Hideaki's troops,

02:21.620 --> 02:27.540
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and
Ishida Mitsunari achieved a sweeping victory,

02:27.540 --> 02:33.800
bringing what should have been
three hundred years of peace to the world.

02:34.630 --> 02:39.680
You should all be quite familiar with this story...

02:46.730 --> 02:49.940
Master Takuan

02:58.830 --> 03:04.790
Shijou-no-yado Inn

03:07.920 --> 03:09.840
That's weird.

03:09.840 --> 03:13.920
There should have been someone who said they saw Musashi around here.

03:27.980 --> 03:29.860
Was I imagining things?

03:34.110 --> 03:38.070
Woman, you are looking for Miyamoto Musashi?

03:38.320 --> 03:40.620
Who are you?

03:40.620 --> 03:42.370
An acquaintance of Musashi.

03:43.450 --> 03:46.000
He is currently at a certain temple.

03:46.000 --> 03:48.460
I can show you the way.

03:48.460 --> 03:51.210
I would really love to take you up on that,

03:51.210 --> 03:52.880
but I'll have to pass.

03:52.880 --> 03:54.170
Why?

03:54.840 --> 03:56.920
Because you're an ayakashi!

03:57.800 --> 04:03.310
I don't know why you want to lead me to Musashi,

04:03.850 --> 04:06.270
but I will be the one to take Musashi's life!

04:06.270 --> 04:09.440
I'm not gonna let some ayakashi get in the way!

04:09.440 --> 04:12.940
You are spirited. I like you.

04:14.440 --> 04:17.240
I don't care if a monster likes me!

04:17.820 --> 04:20.320
If you don't want a hole in your head,

04:20.320 --> 04:23.910
take that weird face of yours and get lost.

04:25.240 --> 04:29.670
It is no use. You are not capable of killing me.

04:38.300 --> 04:42.220
Normal bullets don't work after all, huh?

04:42.800 --> 04:45.430
Then how about these?

04:46.220 --> 04:50.390
These are ghostbusting bullets I bought from a church in England.

04:50.390 --> 04:54.440
I'm not sure if they work on Japanese ayakashi, but...

05:06.200 --> 05:09.500
I said that I'd lead you to Musashi.

05:09.500 --> 05:12.170
Just be obedient and follow.

05:13.080 --> 05:14.630
I failed!

05:14.630 --> 05:18.970
To think that <i>I</i>... would lose to ayakashi powers...

06:13.770 --> 06:15.520
You are skilled in the ceremony.

06:16.150 --> 06:19.110
How is Musashi-dono?

06:19.110 --> 06:23.530
He is sulking over not being able to train under you.

06:25.530 --> 06:27.700
Such a child.

06:28.450 --> 06:32.910
That old man. He's clearly Takuan,

06:32.910 --> 06:35.710
but he still says that the master is out.

06:35.710 --> 06:37.080
What's with that?

06:37.460 --> 06:39.210
This is a waste of time.

06:53.730 --> 06:55.390
Amazing.

06:56.400 --> 06:57.980
You were here?

06:59.360 --> 07:01.190
These bullet marks...

07:02.570 --> 07:03.570
Indeed.

07:04.070 --> 07:09.490
They are the sweat and blood of those who have mastered gun-dou.

07:10.240 --> 07:12.700
Did <i>he</i> train here?

07:13.330 --> 07:14.370
"He"?

07:14.830 --> 07:18.540
I'm talking about that smug showoff.

07:18.540 --> 07:21.590
Wait, smug showoff?

07:22.050 --> 07:24.670
He has hair <i>this</i> long,

07:24.670 --> 07:26.880
a sword <i>this</i> long,

07:26.880 --> 07:30.510
and a gun <i>this</i> long. That guy!

07:31.890 --> 07:34.520
So you are familiar with Kojiro-dono?

07:34.520 --> 07:36.480
Yeah, I am.

07:36.480 --> 07:39.980
When I just hear his name,

07:39.980 --> 07:42.780
I start feeling a pain right around here.

07:43.150 --> 07:45.190
Sasaki Kojiro...

07:45.190 --> 07:46.990
That name takes me back.

07:48.160 --> 07:54.160
Yes, Sasaki Kojiro-dono, too, once trained in this dojo.

07:57.750 --> 07:59.130
Master Takuan!

07:59.130 --> 08:00.540
...no, Master!

08:00.540 --> 08:03.960
Please, teach me everything there is to know about gun-dou!

08:04.590 --> 08:07.470
Don't make me repeat myself.

08:08.430 --> 08:11.140
I have told you that Master Takuan is gone.

08:11.140 --> 08:14.220
It's obvious that you're the master!

08:14.890 --> 08:16.350
You don't understand?

08:16.350 --> 08:18.310
Takuan will not return.

08:18.940 --> 08:22.190
The one who stands before you is only Master Shibazuke!

08:22.190 --> 08:24.690
You're not making any sense!

08:25.320 --> 08:29.320
When he lost to Sasaki Kojiro, Takuan left on a journey.

08:29.910 --> 08:32.160
One from which he will never return.

08:34.080 --> 08:35.200
Lost— Old man, you lost to him?

08:37.660 --> 08:39.000
Indeed.

08:39.670 --> 08:44.630
Ever since that battle, Takuan has never returned to this temple.

08:44.630 --> 08:46.170
So it had to be.

08:46.170 --> 08:47.970
Why's that?

08:47.970 --> 08:51.550
Those were the terms of the battle.

08:51.550 --> 08:55.470
The one who lost was to forfeit his mastery of gun-dou.

08:55.850 --> 08:58.430
With those terms...

09:00.100 --> 09:01.770
it was a one-on-one battle.

09:28.340 --> 09:29.470
And then...

09:31.130 --> 09:32.680
What more is there to tell?

09:33.090 --> 09:37.260
As I said, Kojiro won, and I lost.

09:50.690 --> 09:52.950
The scent of a woman.

10:06.000 --> 10:07.500
Daitokuji...

10:08.250 --> 10:10.050
Musashi is here.

10:23.770 --> 10:24.980
Halt!

10:24.980 --> 10:28.270
It is forbidden for women to enter this place.

10:28.270 --> 10:31.320
There should be someone called Musashi here.

10:31.320 --> 10:33.860
You are a friend of Musashi?

10:33.860 --> 10:35.780
No, he's no friend of mine.

10:36.200 --> 10:39.410
Musashi... He is the killer...

10:39.410 --> 10:41.700
of my dearest father.

10:42.580 --> 10:44.620
Bring out Musashi!

10:44.620 --> 10:47.710
If you don't, I'll break your neck!

10:52.170 --> 10:53.420
This is bad!

10:53.420 --> 10:56.430
There is a foreign woman who seeks revenge on Musashi!

10:56.890 --> 10:58.260
What?

10:58.260 --> 11:00.140
A foreign woman?

11:00.510 --> 11:04.190
Oh, her again? Good grief.

11:04.190 --> 11:07.350
She followed me here, of all places.

11:07.350 --> 11:11.480
Musashi-dono, you know who this woman is?

11:11.480 --> 11:15.240
Yeah, Desperado's got some kind of misunderstanding.

11:15.240 --> 11:18.700
She thinks I killed her dad, but I never did.

11:18.700 --> 11:22.410
Keeps on following me, going on and on about revenge.

11:22.410 --> 11:24.290
So tired of it.

11:24.290 --> 11:29.130
Oh, the woman is called Desperado?

11:29.130 --> 11:30.170
Yeah.

11:30.170 --> 11:31.420
Musashi-dono!

11:31.420 --> 11:35.300
You should know that women are forbidden in this temple!

11:35.300 --> 11:38.090
Sorry, but I can't help it!

11:38.090 --> 11:40.930
She came here on her own!

11:40.930 --> 11:42.180
Musashi-dono!

11:42.930 --> 11:46.060
Like I said, she came on her own!

11:46.060 --> 11:49.520
Alright, alright, I'll chase her out,

11:49.520 --> 11:51.400
so don't make that face.

11:52.150 --> 11:56.240
I will drive away the foreign woman.

11:56.240 --> 11:59.490
Master, this is too trivial a matter for you to bother with!

11:59.490 --> 12:01.030
Let us take care of it...

12:01.030 --> 12:02.330
Silence!

12:02.660 --> 12:04.330
Excuse my rudeness!

12:04.330 --> 12:08.460
Say, does the master hate women?

12:08.460 --> 12:12.250
Women are absolutely forbidden from entering this temple.

12:12.250 --> 12:14.800
The reason is that Master Takuan—

12:14.800 --> 12:18.510
I mean, Master Shibazuke...

12:19.010 --> 12:21.800
Talking too much can be fatal, you know.

12:22.140 --> 12:23.600
I am sorry!

12:25.060 --> 12:26.230
Hey, old man,

12:26.230 --> 12:28.690
you're up against a girl,

12:28.690 --> 12:31.060
so don't go all-out.

12:31.060 --> 12:33.360
That is not your business.

12:35.610 --> 12:36.860
I will go.

12:38.400 --> 12:40.860
Do I have to go too?

12:40.860 --> 12:42.620
I'm not good at dealing with her.

12:44.200 --> 12:45.870
Leave it to me.

12:53.000 --> 12:57.920
Hey, why does he hate women so much?

12:57.920 --> 13:02.260
If it wasn't for <i>that</i>, he could have won against Sasaki Kojiro.

13:06.850 --> 13:08.430
What are you doing?

13:08.430 --> 13:10.980
Hurry up and bring out Musashi.

13:10.980 --> 13:12.520
Help...

13:13.400 --> 13:17.070
If he doesn't come out, this guy's neck just might snap.

13:17.070 --> 13:19.490
We will not hold back against a woman!

13:19.490 --> 13:21.570
Oh? What are you gonna do?

13:21.990 --> 13:23.910
That's enough.

13:31.330 --> 13:32.960
Ronin?

13:32.960 --> 13:35.540
You really are stubborn.

13:35.540 --> 13:41.550
How many times does Musashi have to tell you that he didn't kill your father?

13:41.760 --> 13:45.350
You can't fool me with those lies!

13:47.970 --> 13:52.230
If you're going to hide him, I'll just find him myself!

13:52.230 --> 13:55.360
You... Are you really Desperado?

14:02.660 --> 14:03.830
Wait!

14:04.540 --> 14:05.960
Master!

14:08.920 --> 14:14.640
Yes, Musashi is my guest here, and he is resting inside.

14:15.430 --> 14:16.890
So he <i>is</i> here.

14:20.930 --> 14:24.560
However, he is very tired...

14:24.560 --> 14:28.820
...and he says he does not wish to see you.

14:30.940 --> 14:35.280
So, as Musashi-dono's teacher,

14:35.280 --> 14:39.870
I, Takuan, will speak to you in his stead.

14:41.450 --> 14:43.830
When did you become Musashi's teacher?

14:45.500 --> 14:47.290
Talk is useless!

14:50.380 --> 14:53.170
Good length and slenderness...

14:53.720 --> 14:55.930
You have good control over your ankles.

14:58.390 --> 15:00.140
Excellent.

15:02.980 --> 15:05.810
Back to the matter, foreign woman,

15:06.310 --> 15:10.070
Japanese temples have certain customs.

15:10.650 --> 15:15.490
It is forbidden for women to enter this one.

15:15.950 --> 15:18.740
It would be best for you to leave.

15:18.740 --> 15:20.200
No way!

15:20.200 --> 15:24.160
I'm not leaving until I get to Musashi!

15:30.420 --> 15:34.590
It seems we cannot reach an understanding through words.

15:42.850 --> 15:45.560
The foreign woman and Master Takuan are...!

15:58.360 --> 16:01.200
My, my... How strange.

16:02.240 --> 16:05.330
The ayakashi presence seems different from usual.

16:05.330 --> 16:08.250
I wonder why that is.

16:10.250 --> 16:12.630
Ah, yes. Let us hurry!

16:30.560 --> 16:32.770
Watch this.

16:32.770 --> 16:34.190
But...

16:34.190 --> 16:36.190
Master Takuan is fighting.

16:39.660 --> 16:43.030
Wow, not a single wasted movement.

16:43.030 --> 16:44.990
As expected of Master Takuan.

16:45.700 --> 16:49.290
Hey, was Desperado always that strong?

16:50.500 --> 16:53.000
She seems different from usual.

16:53.290 --> 16:55.300
Don't look down on me, old man!

16:58.130 --> 16:59.510
You...

16:59.510 --> 17:01.510
You are quite skilled,

17:01.510 --> 17:02.890
but what a shame.

17:03.470 --> 17:05.970
You are backed by another, are you not?

17:05.970 --> 17:08.770
That second party should desist!

17:10.310 --> 17:12.310
For the sake of this woman,

17:12.310 --> 17:14.610
I must lend my assistance!

17:16.730 --> 17:17.990
I'll borrow this.

17:24.240 --> 17:26.030
That dance...!

17:26.030 --> 17:27.290
Dance?

17:27.290 --> 17:28.870
It has revived!

17:28.870 --> 17:32.330
Takuan-sama has revived the Gun-dou Dance!

17:33.000 --> 17:34.790
Gun-dou Dance?

17:35.380 --> 17:38.420
Ever since he lost to Sasaki Kojiro,

17:38.420 --> 17:40.300
it has remained sealed.

17:40.300 --> 17:42.720
The mythical Gun-dou Dance!

17:43.260 --> 17:45.890
Gun-dou Secret Art: Dance of Revelation!

17:47.470 --> 17:50.350
Gun-dou Secret Art, Dance of Revelation?

17:50.350 --> 17:53.770
What are you up to? How foolish!

18:15.580 --> 18:16.920
What is that?

18:17.250 --> 18:18.500
An ayakashi?

18:18.920 --> 18:20.550
What?

18:20.550 --> 18:24.380
This was possessing Desperado.

18:25.890 --> 18:27.220
What for?

18:28.060 --> 18:34.650
I believe it was trying to hide its presence
in order to kill Musashi after lowering his guard.

18:35.600 --> 18:37.610
An ayakashi!

18:37.610 --> 18:38.650
This is bad!

18:38.650 --> 18:40.280
Don't panic.

18:40.280 --> 18:42.490
I'll take it out right now.

18:55.960 --> 18:57.000
Huh?

19:06.300 --> 19:07.840
It got bigger.

19:08.510 --> 19:10.060
I will cut it down.

19:21.980 --> 19:23.740
What's happening?

19:24.110 --> 19:27.610
Both onmyoudan and Meiretsu have no effect...

19:43.300 --> 19:44.630
A spider?

19:44.630 --> 19:47.180
But it has the head and body of a woman.

19:47.550 --> 19:51.140
This is the Demon-Puppeteer Spider Queen.

19:51.140 --> 19:53.140
You know what this is?

19:53.470 --> 19:57.730
The rumors say that it manipulates humans with devilish strings,

19:58.060 --> 20:00.310
a spider ayakashi of the underworld.

20:07.780 --> 20:09.320
What is happening?

20:09.820 --> 20:14.370
Meiretsu, forged from ayakashi bone, has no effect...

20:27.340 --> 20:31.890
That inventor ripped me off again, huh?

20:32.510 --> 20:36.100
No, the Demon-Puppeteer Spider Queen cannot be harmed

20:36.100 --> 20:38.810
with ordinary anti-ayakashi weapons.

20:38.810 --> 20:39.980
What?

20:40.350 --> 20:44.900
Long ago, in an attempt to save a young man who had fallen to hell,

20:44.900 --> 20:48.860
the Buddha in heaven took a spider from a lotus

20:48.860 --> 20:54.030
and let down a single spider thread.

20:55.160 --> 20:58.330
The young man took hold of the string,

20:58.330 --> 21:00.920
and ascended toward heaven...

21:01.790 --> 21:09.300
...but others in hell had also clung to it,

21:09.720 --> 21:11.510
and the young man...

21:13.510 --> 21:19.020
...fell down to hell with the others.

21:20.440 --> 21:21.980
When that happened,

21:21.980 --> 21:24.730
the involved spider that fell into hell

21:25.150 --> 21:27.780
eventually became a demon.

21:27.780 --> 21:32.530
That spider was originally from heaven,

21:32.530 --> 21:36.030
so weapons made for ayakashi will not work.

21:36.450 --> 21:41.120
This is the Demon-Puppeteer Spider Queen...

21:43.630 --> 21:46.460
I see you know my story well.

21:46.460 --> 21:49.380
In return for that introduction,

21:49.380 --> 21:53.840
I will show you the true extent of my powers!

21:54.850 --> 21:55.800
Oh no!

21:55.800 --> 21:56.560
Run!

22:01.770 --> 22:02.890
These strings!

22:02.890 --> 22:04.020
They won't break!

22:05.480 --> 22:07.440
So loud...

22:07.690 --> 22:09.610
Hey, where am I?

22:11.190 --> 22:12.490
Musashi!

22:12.900 --> 22:14.780
For my father!

22:15.700 --> 22:17.780
You idiot! Look at what's happening!

22:17.780 --> 22:19.040
What's happening?

22:19.040 --> 22:23.370
Right, I was in the city, so how did I...

22:23.370 --> 22:26.920
Oh, where did that ayakashi go?

22:32.470 --> 22:34.430
What's with these strings?

22:34.430 --> 22:35.720
Desperado!

22:35.720 --> 22:39.100
We have to do something, Master Takuan!

22:42.980 --> 22:45.270
It is time...

22:45.980 --> 22:50.230
...to show you my signature skill!

22:58.660 --> 23:00.830
My body is moving on its own!

23:05.290 --> 23:07.250
Hey, what are you doing?

23:07.830 --> 23:09.880
It's not me!

23:10.210 --> 23:12.760
Demon-Puppeteer Spider Queen.

23:12.760 --> 23:14.670
They say it uses the strings it spits out

23:14.670 --> 23:18.930
to control the movements of humans like puppets.

23:18.930 --> 23:20.890
So it was true...

23:23.890 --> 23:26.230
Not only do the onmyoudan not work,

23:26.230 --> 23:29.440
but it's putting me up against someone I don't want to fight!

23:29.440 --> 23:30.860
What am I supposed to do?

23:39.990 --> 23:42.200
Somebody stop me!

23:51.420 --> 23:52.710
Damn it...

23:52.710 --> 23:56.420
What am I supposed to do!?

24:00.600 --> 24:03.350
In my natural, unadorned style,

24:03.350 --> 24:06.180
I'll tell you these feelings of mine

24:06.180 --> 24:11.520
Together to the sky past the darkness!

24:11.520 --> 24:16.650
All we need to do is spread our wings and fly!

24:18.200 --> 24:23.330
Baby, we'll send time flowing forward just a little,

24:23.330 --> 24:29.500
and we'll embrace even the harsh gusts of wind

24:29.500 --> 24:34.840
with sympathy for pointless worries

24:34.840 --> 24:38.970
and a melody that will overcome the pain

24:41.340 --> 24:51.730
If the poison of the flower that bloomed in my cupped hands

24:51.730 --> 25:02.660
has managed to pierce through the center of my heart...

25:02.660 --> 25:05.410
In my natural, unadorned style,

25:05.410 --> 25:08.290
I'll tell you these feelings of mine,

25:08.290 --> 25:13.880
Unraveling this puzzle of the heart

25:13.880 --> 25:16.630
I'll bring out every part

25:16.630 --> 25:19.630
of your unchanging style

25:19.630 --> 25:24.930
Together to the sky past the darkness!

25:24.930 --> 25:30.100
All we need to do is spread our wings and fly!

25:31.560 --> 25:34.400
What's up with that spider monster?

25:34.400 --> 25:36.570
It's way too strong!

25:36.570 --> 25:38.820
Hey, Inventor!

25:38.820 --> 25:41.150
Do you have something good?

25:41.150 --> 25:47.540
The next chapter: <i>The Demon Gun</i>!
